  clock: 25  # 99a1
  nonce: 99a1  # 99a1
  message: "CLAUSE (a3) IS MET as of PR #204 (dev 427f47f6b1). ITEM STAYS VIOLATED --\n(a1) is unaddressed (Phase 5 matching), (a2) remains vacuously true while\nADR-0017 section 3a is confirm-only, and (b) holds only with the three limits\nalready filed. Closing on one clause would be a partition dressed as a\nresolution (L14), which this item's own history has been corrected for twice.\n\nWHAT (a3) DEMANDED, AND WHY IT WAS NOT MET IN EITHER HALF.\n\nThe clause has two halves: a reader must tell data-flow-adjudicated flows from\ncall-reachability-only ones FROM THE EMITTED RECORD, and the scope of\ndata-flow coverage may not be left to assumption.\n\nHALF ONE WAS NOT MERELY MISSING, IT WAS WRONG. The field carrying the\ndistinction, TaintFlowFinding.analysis_method, was not a property of the flow.\ncmd_verify_claims builds one DDG for the whole repository and then dispatches\nper language on \"if ddg_edges:\" -- a repo-global truthiness test -- so every\nlanguage ran through propagate_taint_ddg whenever ANY language produced DDG\nedges. A JavaScript function is never in ddg_symbols (JavaScript has no\ndef/use extractor), so the walk could not run, and the finding still came out\nddg_mixed, whose documented meaning is \"the walk ran and did not confirm\".\n\nBEHAVIOURAL REPRO, two repos whose JavaScript is byte-identical, differing by\none unrelated src/util.py:\n\n  hypergumbo verify-claims <repo> --claims claims.yaml --json\n  claim: untrusted_input -> host_fs\n  fixture: http.createServer() -> fs.writeFileSync(), both module-qualified\n           and absent from javascript ambiguous_names\n\n  js only        exit 1, 1 flow, analysis_method = structural\n  js + util.py   exit 1, 1 flow, analysis_method = ddg_mixed\n\nSame flow, same evidence row in every other field. The diff was exactly the\ntwo lines carrying the label. A reader cannot tell the two apart when the\ndistinguishing field is set by an unrelated language's presence.\n\nFIXED by choosing the label on whether the DDG actually covered the source\nfunction (fn_has_ddg), which is what analysis_method's own docstring has always\nsaid structural meant: \"no reaching-def data ... so no walk was possible\".\nPinned by a red-first unit test and a two-arm end-to-end test asserting the\nwhole record is identical across arms, not just the label.\n\nWHY NO TEST CAUGHT THIS: all five existing tests asserting ddg_mixed place the\nsource function inside ddg_symbols, so fn_has_ddg was true in every one. The\ncontaminated case had no test anywhere.\n\nHALF TWO: the scope is now emitted as data. verify-claims carries a\ndataflow_coverage block (envelope schema 1.6 -> 1.7, additive) on the JSON\nsurface and rendered on the TEXT surface, with one row per analyzed language\ncarrying its catalog counts and four independent capability bits --\ncfg_mapping, atomic_statement, def_use_extractor, ddg_spec -- plus\ndataflow_capable (their conjunction) and blockers (the missing ones, so a row\nsays what to fix). Four bits rather than one flag because each is\nindividually sufficient to keep the machinery silently inert: Rust shipped an\nextractor in March and emitted zero DDG edges for months while failing three\nat once, and Java ships cfg_nodes/java.yaml while declaring no\natomic_statement and registering no extractor.\n\nTWO DECLARED CONSTANTS STATE WHAT NO PER-RUN MEASUREMENT CAN.\n\n  inclusion_decided_by = call_graph_reachability. Section 3a is confirm-only,\n  so every reported flow INCLUDING every ddg-labelled one was included by\n  call-graph BFS. This is clause (a2)'s vacuity made non-assumable, and it is\n  the executable re-evaluation trigger R16 requires: when 3a gains refutation\n  the constant must change or its test fails.\n\n  coverage_granularity = language. Capability is NOT a per-function\n  completeness claim. cfg_nodes/go.yaml self-documents that\n  \"if err := do(); err != nil\" initializers are invisible to def/use, so a\n  capable language still holds functions the walk cannot see into. WI-joluk is\n  the finer signal; when it lands this becomes \"function\".\n\nMEASURED WITH PRODUCTION LOADERS, NOT RE-DERIVED (L53). Counts come from\nload_builtin_taint_catalog, load_cfg_mapping, get_def_use_extractor and\nregistered_ddg_languages, never from a hand-written predicate:\n\n  553 sources, 1062 sinks, 12 sanitizers, 15 languages\n  274 sinks (25.8%) sit in a data-flow-capable language (go, python, rust,\n  typescript)\n\nThe campaign plan recorded 244 / 23%. Rust's 30 joined when WI-tohuk landed\natomic_statement -- exactly the drift a computed table removes, which is the\nargument for emitting the scope rather than writing it down. TypeScript is\nfully capable and has ZERO sinks, so the 274 come from three languages; Java's\n69 are the largest block behind a language that looks supported."  # 99a1
