  by: agent  # 49d5
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 49d5
  clock: 31  # 49d5
  nonce: 49d5  # 49d5
  message: "SPOT-CHECKED 2026-08-09 during a staleness sweep of the taint/CFG/dataflow items.\nNO CORRECTION MADE, and I am recording the LIMIT of what I checked rather than\nimplying a clean bill.\n\nWHAT I CHECKED: this item's thread is current (2026-08-08 unconfounded\nre-measurement), its statement clauses read consistently with that entry, and its\nheadline numbers are already heavily caveated in place -- the 16.7% precision\ndatapoint carries its own 'do NOT quote this' warning and names the 70.3%\nunadjudicated denominator, and clause (b)'s zero is already flagged as latent\nrather than live.\n\nWHAT I DID NOT DO: I did not re-run any of this item's repros, and I did not\nre-derive the precision sample. So this note is NOT evidence that the item's\nmeasurements still hold -- only that its text is internally consistent with its most\nrecent measurement and carries no citation I could show to be dead.\n\nFour sibling items in the same sweep DID need correction (INV-busis title, INV-sadah\nroot_cause identifiers, INV-fokik mechanism relocation, WI-joluk description), so\n'the thread is recent' was not a reliable proxy for 'the fields are current'. If this\nitem is picked up, re-run its repros first."  # 49d5
- op: discuss  # c0e2
  at: '2026-08-21T19:10:00Z'  # c0e2
  by: agent  # c0e2
  actor: jgstern_agent  # c0e2
  clock: 32  # c0e2
  nonce: c0e2  # c0e2
  message: "CLAUSE (a2) VIOLATED LIVE, WITH AN ISOLATED REPRO, 2026-08-21, dev 09921c57a1.\nFound while diagnosing INV-rozob, whose \"multiplier\" evidence is this clause.\n\n(a2) requires: for a flow whose source and sink call sites lie in the SAME\nfunction AND whose function has data-dependence coverage, a reaching-definition\nchain must exist from the variable the source defines to a use at the sink call\nsite. It does not.\n\nTHE REPRO. One file, one function_declaration -- which is the ONLY node type the\njavascript/typescript DDG spec enters, so this function IS data-dependence\ncovered, not a scope-gap case:\n\n    function f() {\n      const a = navigator.userAgent; console.log(a);\n      const b = window.screen;       console.warn(b);\n    }\n\n    claim: source_taint host_secret, prohibited_sink_zone logging\n    RESULT: 4 flows, all analysis_method=\"ddg_mixed\"\n\nTwo of the four -- a -> warn and b -> log -- have NO reaching-definition chain.\nEvery source in the symbol is paired with every sink in the symbol.\n\nSTRONGER ARM, where the sink provably cannot receive the value:\n\n    function f() {\n      const a = navigator.userAgent; console.log(a);\n      const b = window.screen;       console.warn(\"literal\");\n    }\n    RESULT: 4 flows. Precision 1/4.\n\n`b` is defined and never used at any sink; `console.warn` receives a string\nliteral. Three of the four reported flows are refutable from the four lines.\n\nIT SCALES MULTIPLICATIVELY, measured rather than asserted -- 1 source/1 sink -> 1\nflow; 2/2 -> 4; 3/3 -> 9. The row count is |sources| x |sinks| within the symbol,\nso it scales with the CATALOGUE, not with the code. INV-rozob makes the same\npoint from the other end: adding a seventh browser global to the catalogue would\nadd three more \"violations\" to a repo whose source did not change.\n\nNOT A SCOPE GAP, AND THIS IS THE PART THAT SURPRISED ME. I expected the cause to\nbe the DDG's narrow scope (ts_def_use registers function_node_types =\n{\"function_declaration\"} only, and on mitmproxy's web tree 80.4% of JS/TS\ncallables are something else -- arrow_function 69.0%, method_definition 5.9%,\nfunction_expression 5.5%). It is not. A/B over the three shapes, same 3-source\n3-sink body in each:\n\n    function_declaration   9 flows   ddg_mixed     <- DDG-covered, SAME count\n    arrow_function         9 flows   structural\n    method_definition      9 flows   structural\n\nWidening the DDG scope would convert `structural` to `ddg_mixed` and move ZERO\nfindings. I nearly shipped that fix; the A/B is the only reason I did not, and it\nis recorded here so the next reader does not re-derive it. The defect is in what\nthe ddg_mixed / structural arms EMIT, not in which functions they reach.\n\nWHERE IT LIVES. propagate_taint_structural (taint.py ~2058) loops\n`for caller_id, source_callee_id, taint_source in source_callers:` and then, per\nseed, `for sink_node, sink_callee_id, taint_sink in _iter_sink_sites(...)`,\nappending one TaintFlowFinding per reachable pair. The DDG arm has the same shape\naround taint.py ~3011. Neither consults a reaching-definition chain before\nemitting when the walk did not confirm one -- which is precisely what\nanalysis_method=\"ddg_mixed\" means (\"the walk ran without confirming a\ndependence\").\n\nDIRECTION FOR A FIX, NOT PRICED AND NOT CHOSEN. An unconfirmed analysis cannot\nhonestly claim \"primitive P1 reached primitive P2\"; what it can claim is \"symbol\nS reads {P1..Pn} and reaches zone Z via {Q1..Qm}\". Emitting one finding per\n(source_symbol, taint_label, sink_zone) with the primitives as SETS would make\nthe count scale with code. That changes finding SHAPE and therefore counts in\nevery language and every consumer, so it wants an A/B on findings, both signs,\nbefore anyone touches it -- the INV-nizom shape (a consumer rule that looked\nobviously correct removed 51 io-boundary matches, 49 of them TRUE).\n\nNOT MEASURED: how much of the ~41% population-weighted precision figure in\ndocs/measurements/0001 is this mechanism. That is the number that decides whether\nthis is the headline lever of the <50% band or one of several. It is answerable\nby re-adjudicating 0001's census with pair-collapse applied."  # c0e2
- op: discuss  # 86cd
  at: '2026-08-22T01:30:37Z'  # 86cd
  by: agent  # 86cd
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 86cd
  clock: 33  # 86cd
  nonce: 86cd  # 86cd
  message: "THE NUMBER THIS ITEM NAMED AS NOT MEASURED, MEASURED. 2026-08-21, dev a34daf706f,\n6 repos, every distinct violating flow verify-claims reports for the six generic\nclaims. The item asked: \"how much of the ~41% population-weighted precision\nfigure in docs/measurements/0001 is this mechanism. That is the number that\ndecides whether this is the headline lever of the <50% band.\"\n\n    repo         flows  situations  collapse   size distribution\n    caddy          219          21    10.43x   1x3, 3x1, 6x2, 8x1, 10x8, 11x1, 13x2\n    sops            39          11     3.55x   1x6, 2x1, 3x1, 5x1, 10x1, 13x1\n    poetry          13           5     2.60x   1x1, 2x1, 3x2, 4x1\n    mitmproxy       60          26     2.31x   1x14, 2x6, 3x3, 4x1, 8x1, 13x1\n    knex            25          12     2.08x   1x7, 2x3, 4x1, 8x1\n    express          3           3     1.00x   1x3\n    TOTAL          359          78     4.60x\n\nA \"situation\" is (source_symbol, claim) -- claim fixes the taint label and the\nsink zone, so this is exactly the (source_symbol, taint_label, sink_zone) key the\nDIRECTION section of this item proposed emitting one finding per.\n\n*** 281 OF 359 REPORTED ROWS (78%) ARE ADDITIONAL ROWS ABOUT A SITUATION ALREADY\nREPORTED. *** On caddy one symbol -- cmd/commandfuncs.go cmdRun -- produces 76\nrows across three claims (32 + 22 + 22).\n\nTHE INSTRUMENT WAS CHECKED BEFORE THE NUMBER WAS BELIEVED. _MAX_EVIDENCE_ROWS\nhead-truncates the evidence list at 100 and would have understated the ratio;\nevery verdict in the cohort has evidence_count == len(evidence), so nothing is\ntruncated and the census is complete rather than a first-hundred sample.\n\n*** AND THERE ARE TWO MULTIPLIERS, WHERE THIS ITEM NAMED ONE. *** Separating them:\n\n    flows / distinct (situation, source_primitive, sink_primitive) = 1.60x\n    pairs / situations                                             = 2.87x\n    flows / situations                                             = 4.60x\n\n2.87x is the |sources| x |sinks| product this item measured synthetically\n(1/1->1, 2/2->4, 3/3->9). The other 1.60x is DUPLICATE PATHS to the SAME\n(source_primitive, sink_primitive) pair -- distinct `path` values make distinct\nrows under _flow_identity. Nobody had named that one, and a fix keyed only on the\npair product would leave it.\n\nSO: YES, THIS IS THE HEADLINE LEVER. For scale, the other mechanism of comparable\nsize in 0001 -- the 19 unadjudicable unanchored-placeholder rows -- was fixed\ntoday (INV-rozob, PR #473).\n\n*** WHAT THIS DOES TO THE BAND'S OWN NUMBER, stated carefully because it must not\nbe used to argue the band down. *** WI-sivuz's bands were named BEFORE any\ninterval was computed, so an interval cannot move them, and that stands. But\n0001's ~41% is a per-ROW precision, and this census shows the row denominator is\n4.60x the situation count on a comparable cohort. Per-SITUATION precision is a\nDIFFERENT quantity that has never been computed, and it is the one a reader\nacts on (\"is this symbol a problem?\" not \"is row 7 of 32 a problem?\"). Which way\nit moves is NOT predictable from here: it depends on whether the large groups\nadjudicate TP or FP, and 0001's 21 co-location-function FPs are exactly the rows\nmost likely to be grouped. Answering it means re-adjudicating 0001's census at\nthe situation level, which is a measurement in its own right and is the honest\nnext step before any claim that precision is better or worse than recorded.\n\nNOT MEASURED: which way per-situation precision moves (above); whether the 1.60x\npath multiplier is ever load-bearing for a reader (two call paths to the same\nprimitive pair may or may not be worth two rows -- I did not adjudicate any);\nand any language outside the six repos here."  # 86cd
- op: discuss  # 811e
  at: '2026-08-22T03:20:30Z'  # 811e
  by: agent  # 811e
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 811e
  clock: 34  # 811e
  nonce: 811e  # 811e
  message: "Merged in PR #474 (dev c14cbc2d7f).\n\nCOLLAPSE SHIPPED. The DIRECTION section of this item, built and measured in both\nsigns. Status stays violated: this makes the CLAIM honest, and clause (a2) is\nstill unmet for every unadjudicated flow.\n\nWHAT CHANGED. A finding whose analysis_method is `structural` or `ddg_mixed` was\nincluded because a call path exists, not because a data dependence was shown, so\n\"primitive P1 reached primitive P2\" is more than the analysis established. Such\nfindings are now collapsed to one per situation -- (taint_label, source_symbol,\nsink_zone, sanitized, source_boundary, analysis_method) -- carrying\nsource_primitives / sink_primitives / sink_symbols as MODULE-QUALIFIED sets:\n\"symbol S reads {P..Pn} and reaches zone Z via {Q..Qm}\". Qualified because `Do`\nis not checkable against a catalogue and `net/http.Client.Do` is (clause a1).\n\nBOTH MULTIPLIERS DIE, which is why the key names NEITHER primitive. A key built\non the pair would have left the 1.60x duplicate-route multiplier standing.\n\nTWO DEPARTURES FROM THIS ITEM'S OWN PROPOSAL, both priced before taking them.\n\n(1) ADJUDICATED FLOWS ARE NOT COLLAPSED. `ddg` means the SS3a walk confirmed a\nreaching-def chain from the variable the source defines to a use at the sink call\nsite -- that IS a pair claim. Measured share of the census before deciding: 6 of\n359 flows, 1.7%. Collapsing them would trade earned precision for almost none of\nthe noise. caddy's printEnvironment is the illustration: it now reports\nos.Getwd -> fmt.Printf as an adjudicated PAIR and {os.Environ, os.Getwd,\nruntime.GOARCH, runtime.GOOS} -> {fmt.Printf, fmt.Println} as a 7-pair situation,\nside by side.\n\n(2) THE KEY CARRIES TWO FIELDS THIS ITEM DID NOT NAME. `sanitized`, because a\nsanitized flow is excluded from the violation set and a mixed group would have to\nbe counted both ways. `source_boundary`, because WI-vazal split net_recv /\nipc_recv / db_read INSIDE the single untrusted_input label precisely so \"a\nrequest body reached the database\" stays separable from \"a row read from the\ndatabase reached the database\" -- merging across it would undo that.\n\nTheir presence is also what makes collapsing BEFORE the consumer's filters sound,\nand this is the load-bearing argument rather than a convenience: every filter\nverify_taint_claim applies -- label, zone, `sanitized`, and _source_scope's\nproduction test, which reads source_symbol and nothing else -- tests a field that\nis IN the key. So no group can be half-included. Asserted by a test, not left as\nreasoning.\n\nA/B, BOTH SIGNS, per the INV-nizom precedent. Arms differing only in this change;\nsame six repos at the same checkouts; same claims file; per-arm XDG_CACHE_HOME;\narm A a detached worktree at the parent commit, asserted to LACK the collapse\nbefore any measurement (3 occurrences vs 0). Evidence completeness asserted first\n-- evidence_count == len(evidence) on every verdict in BOTH arms -- so the\ncoverage check ran over the whole population and not a first-hundred slice.\n\n    repo         rows A -> situations B   ratio\n    caddy               219 ->  23        9.52x\n    sops                 39 ->  11        3.55x\n    poetry               13 ->   5        2.60x\n    mitmproxy            60 ->  26        2.31x\n    knex                 25 ->  12        2.08x\n    express               3 ->   3        1.00x\n    TOTAL               359 ->  80        4.49x\n\n  VERDICT MOVES: 0.   ARM-A (source_symbol, source_primitive, sink_primitive,\n  sink_symbol) TUPLES MISSING FROM ARM B: 0.\n\n80 rather than the census's 78 because this key is FINER than the census's\n(source_symbol, claim): the extra two are boundary/method splits. So 4.49x is\nCONSERVATIVE against the census's 4.60x, not a disagreement with it.\n\nTHE PAIR COUNT IS DISCLOSED, NOT TRADED AWAY. `details` gains a\n\"spanning N source->sink pair(s)\" clause -- silent when it equals the situation\ncount, so a single-pair verdict stays byte-identical -- and every evidence row\ncarries collapsed_flow_count. The total is computed over ALL violations rather\nthan summed across the evidence list, because that list is capped at\n_MAX_EVIDENCE_ROWS and the sum would be wrong above it.\n\nENVELOPE 2.0 -> 2.1. Not purely additive and deliberately so, on the 1.5\nprecedent: evidence_count and the details count now report SITUATIONS. The\nwitness scalars keep their names and stay valid (each is a member of its own\nset), so nothing a 2.0 consumer reads disappears.\n\nONE STALE READER FOUND, and it was a mock that could not have been wrong about\nanything else. test_cfg.py's _MockTaintFinding hand-restated nine of the\ndataclass's fields and raised AttributeError the moment it gained sink_symbols;\nit now constructs the real dataclass. cfg.select_ddg_targets itself read the\nwitness sink_symbol and now reads the set -- honest scope: that function has NO\nproduction caller today, so this is a latent reader corrected, not an observed\nregression.\n\nWHAT THIS DOES NOT CLOSE. Clause (a2) is still unmet for every unadjudicated\nflow, and removal remains UNSOUND on this substrate: the call graph emits one\nedge per (caller, callee), so an edge's `line` is *a* line and not every line\n(printEnvironment calls fmt.Printf twelve times; the edge records the first).\nThat is why the DDG arm is confirm-only by design and why (a2) cannot be met by\ndropping flows without inventing false negatives. Clause (a1)'s file-path-in-the-\nmodule-slot residual (WI-damir) is untouched. And which way PER-SITUATION\nprecision moves is still not measured -- that is the next step in this chain and\na measurement in its own right."  # 811e
- op: discuss  # 560c
  at: '2026-08-22T03:32:37Z'  # 560c
  by: agent  # 560c
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 560c
  clock: 35  # 560c
  nonce: 560c  # 560c
  message: "PER-SITUATION PRECISION MEASURED — the number this item's last entry named as NOT\nMEASURED (\"which way per-situation precision moves\"). Filed as\ndocs/measurements/0004. Status unchanged: violated.\n\n*** IT MOVES UP, AND BY 2.9x. *** Same adjudication, same repositories, same\ncommit; only the unit differs.\n\n    unit                                   TP   population   precision\n    row (source->sink pair, pre-collapse)  33          297      11.1%\n    situation (post-collapse)              19           59      32.2%\n\nMECHANISM: false positives concentrate in the LARGEST groups, which is the\ndirection this item said was not predictable from where it stood. caddy's\ncmd/commandfuncs.go cmdRun emits 76 rows across three claims and every one is\nfalse -- its os.Getenv reads are all compared to \"\" and runtime.GOOS is a\nswitch subject, i.e. control dependence, which 0001's rubric calls FP -- and it\ncollapses to 3 situations. Meanwhile 12 of the 19 TRUE situations stand for a\nsingle pair each. So the collapse removes FP mass faster than TP mass.\n\nPOPULATION: 0001's own CENSUS cohort (caddy, mitmproxy, poetry, express,\napollo-server), every distinct violating record for the six generic claims.\n0001's pretix half deliberately excluded -- it was 77% of that population and\none framework dominated its TPs, so pooling it back would re-import the\nconcentration.\n\nMETHOD LIMIT, STATED FIRST BECAUSE IT IS THE WEAKEST PART. 0001's census used a\nblind second pass by a fresh agent plus a third on disagreement, specifically to\ncontrol the bias it named (\"the census author wrote much of the code being\nmeasured\"). That control is NOT reproduced here: single-pass, non-blind, by the\nauthor of the change being measured. The only mitigation was fixed in advance --\nTIES GO TO FALSE POSITIVE -- so both rates are FLOORS. Admissible as evidence\nabout the DIRECTION and SIZE of the row-vs-situation difference; NOT a\nreplacement for 0001's headline.\n\nAND IT DOES NOT MOVE THE BAND. WI-sivuz's bands were named before any interval\nwas computed. This changes what the number MEASURES, not the ranking rule --\nwhich is what this item's own entry said in advance, and it still holds now that\nthe direction is known rather than guessed.\n\n11.1% is NOT comparable to 0001's 26.2% census rate: the population drifted\n60 -> 298 flows in nine days (0001 records this itself), and 0003 measured a\nrecall widening landing at 2.9% marginal precision. The comparable pair is the\ntwo rows of the table above.\n\nSECONDARY FINDINGS:\n* ZERO unadjudicable, against 19 of 104 in 0001. Every situation named a file a\n  reader could open. NOT offered as INV-rozob evidence -- those file nodes are\n  in-repo anchors the collapse never touched.\n* ddg 80.0% (4/5), structural 33.3% (10/30), ddg_mixed 20.8% (5/24). ddg_mixed\n  BELOW structural is 0001's reversal reproduced in a second population: the\n  label is not a calibrated confidence. And ddg is still too small to filter on\n  -- 5 of 59 situations holding 4 of 19 TPs, so a ddg-only view discards 15 of\n  19 real findings. 0001's DO NOT FILTER ON confidence, at the situation unit.\n* 17 of the 40 FP situations are CONTROL-DEPENDENCE-ONLY, the single largest\n  class, and that is a stated rubric convention rather than a tool defect.\n* 51 of 59 situations are host-secret-*, with sources including runtime.GOOS,\n  platform.system, sys.argv and shutil.get_terminal_size. That is INV-tutar's\n  vocabulary question and it is the biggest lever on this table that is not a\n  precision fix at all."  # 560c
- op: discuss  # 5458
  at: '2026-08-25T20:11:47Z'  # 5458
  by: agent  # 5458
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 5458
  clock: 36  # 5458
  nonce: '5458'  # 5458
  message: "THE TWO-UNIT RESULT REPRODUCES ON A THIRD POPULATION, and 0005 measures the row unit instead of apportioning it. docs/measurements/0005-taint-precision-after-vocabulary-split.md.\n\n0005 (census of 0004's cohort at ba01153095): 21.6% per SITUATION (8 TP of 37) and 10.0% per ROW (17 TP of 170) -- a 2.16x gap, against 0004's 2.9x on its own population. This item's original observation stands: which way per-situation precision moves is not predictable from the collapse alone, and on both populations it moves UP.\n\nWHAT IS NEW IS THE METHOD. 0004 had to hand-block the row unit because a collapsed record reports only HOW MANY pairs it swallowed (collapsed_flow_count), not WHICH -- so a reader cannot adjudicate a swallowed row on its own terms. 0005 added `collect --no-collapse` to the measurement instrument, which rebinds taint.collapse_unadjudicated_flows to the identity for that process only (production untouched), and ran the SAME census twice. The two arms reconcile exactly: 37 situations whose collapsed_flow_count sums to 170, against 170 pair records; every situation's member set recovered (37/37) via the visible half of the collapse key; both ledgers agreeing on TP=17, FP=153. That reconciliation is now a standing control on this collapse -- if a future change to the grouping key breaks it, the two arms stop agreeing.\n\nA CONSEQUENCE OF THE COLLAPSE WORTH RECORDING. A situation is TRUE POSITIVE iff AT LEAST ONE of its pairs is, so a situation label cannot say how many are. The instrument now REFUSES to print a row rate for a multi-pair TP that carries no explicit per-pair count, rather than assuming \"all\" (which inflates) or \"one\" (which deflates).\n\nAND THE MULTIPLIER HAS A THIRD FORM THIS ITEM DID NOT NAME. This item measured 2.87x from the |sources| x |sinks| product inside one symbol and 1.60x from distinct routes to the same pair. 0005 found a third: on caddy the call graph is fully connected through caddy.Load -> changeConfig -> unsyncedDecodeAndRun, so the SAME ten or eleven terminal I/O calls (FileWriter.OpenWriter, InstanceID, exitProcess, acmeserver.openDatabase, httploader, reverseproxy) appear under FOUR different sources in four different packages. One source read buys a fixed tax of about a dozen rows regardless of what it is, and `reachability-only` has consequently overtaken control-dependence as the largest false-positive class (12 of 29 situations, 9 of them caddy). The collapse already absorbs this at the situation unit -- which is exactly why the situation unit is 2.16x better here -- but the row unit still carries it, and any future row-denominated number on a large connected Go repo will be dominated by it."  # 5458
