- op: discuss  # da29
  at: '2026-09-06T15:45:17Z'  # da29
  by: agent  # da29
  actor: jgstern_agent  # da29
  clock: 38  # da29
  nonce: da29  # da29
  message: "RE-CHECKED AT TIP 2026-09-06 (dev 87104c6281), clause by clause, against a LIVE record and against 0012 -- arc stage 5. Status stays violated; this entry records which clauses now hold on evidence and exactly what was NOT re-run, so the next reader does not have to re-derive it.\n\nLIVE RECORD: `hypergumbo verify-claims curriculum_repos/caddy --claims docs/example-claims/generic-taint-claims.yaml --json`, cold cache (scratchpad p7/karud/caddy.json): 153 findings at run level (ddg 10, ddg_mixed 143), 31 evidence rows across 7 violated claims, flows_removed_by_walk 0.\n\n(a1) ATTRIBUTION SOUNDNESS -- HOLDS on the record. Every one of the 148 sink-primitive slots on the 31 rows is module-qualified (`os/exec.Cmd.Start`, `net.Listener.Accept`, `os.WriteFile`), `sink_module` / `source_module` travel on the row, and `sink_symbols` carry the boundary ids the matcher used, so a reader confirms the match by catalogue lookup without re-running the matcher. 148 of 148; the #474 collapse's module-qualified sets are what made this true.\n(a3) PUBLISHED SCOPE -- HOLDS. Each row carries walk_verdict (30 not_attempted, 1 escaped on this record; confirmed where it applies) and walk_blocked_by; the run carries dataflow_coverage.inclusion_decided_by = \"call_graph_reachability_minus_ddg_refutation\" verbatim and findings_by_analysis_method. A reader tells the two adjudication kinds apart from the emitted record.\n(c) HONEST LABELLING -- HOLDS. 31 of 31 rows are confidence=approximate / analysis_method=ddg_mixed; `precise`/`ddg` appears only on walk-confirmed rows (INV-sadah re-verified today on its own repro: an unrelated DDG edge no longer earns the label).\n(a2) DATA-FLOW CONSISTENCY WHERE COVERED -- HOLDS BY CONSTRUCTION FOR WALKED FLOWS SINCE WI-kabif (PR #716): a walk that exhausts every route without a dependence returns False and REMOVES the flow, so no surviving same-function flow with coverage lacks a reaching-def chain. The precondition is what limits it: on this record 30 of 31 rows are not_attempted (source outside a walked function, or no def/use coverage for the language) and 1 escaped, i.e. a2's \"where covered\" applies to almost none of them, and 0012 §\"What this does not support\" says the same about the cohort. That is a3 doing its job, not a2 being met broadly.\n(b) SANITIZER NEUTRALIZATION BY CATEGORY -- NOT RE-RUN TODAY. The 2026-06-09 fix (taint.py _match_propagation sanitizer category check) is present in the tree; no live check of a cross-category barrier was performed in this pass. Stated so it is not read as verified.\n\nTHE FILED REPRO, NOT RE-RUN: the 2026-08-01 violations were bare-name attribution errors on pretix (d3.v6.js `log` matched as a console.log LOGGING sink; d3-dispatch `get` matched as http.get NETWORK). Those are (a1) instances and (a1) now holds on caddy's record by module qualification, but the closure-evidence discipline wants the item's OWN repro re-run: pretix with the generic claims, and the two d3 sites checked for absence. pretix's survey is ~10 minutes and its taint run longer; it was not run in this pass.\n\nAGAINST 0012. The precision band this item's clauses feed is 0012's 34.0% / 30.0% (situation / row) correctness at f247b52587, which lifted the band that held Phase 6 recall; nothing in today's record contradicts 0012's frame, and this item's clause (a2) is the reason the row unit stays disclosed beside the situation unit.\n\nWHAT WOULD MOVE THE STATUS: (1) the pretix repro re-run showing the two d3 sites no longer match (a1 on the item's own population); (2) one live cross-category barrier check for (b). With both, violated -> pending_validation, with 0013 (the next precision measurement) as the validation. PROPOSAL for the owner: schedule those two as the item's next pass rather than more clause prose."  # da29
